WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.418
- If I ever go to his house,
I'm takin' the ball.

00:00:01.418 --> 00:00:02.585
- You gonna steal it?
- Yeah, I'm gonna steal it.

00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:03.878
- Brett, Brett,
hide the ball, man.

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:04.546
- I'm stealin' that, for real.

00:00:04.546 --> 00:00:06.965
- If Sean McVay
has breathed near you

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:09.342
you're gonna be a head coach in the NFL.
- Right.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.261
Troll him, Saints fans!

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:12.971
- Look how dumb he looks in that.

00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:17.600
♪♪♪

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.354
Welcome to "Simms &amp; Lefkoe,"
and it is the best weekend

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.399
of NFL football of the year,
divisional round.

00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:25.734
You've always felt this way?

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.110
- Yes.
I mean, the last two weekends.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.653
I mean, Wild Card Weekend's great.
- Yeah.

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:31.364
- But this one is the one
I really look forward to.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.116
It's the eight best teams
in football.
- Without a doubt.

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:35.452
- And I think we literally
got the eight best in there

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:37.078
this year,
which is refreshing to me.

00:00:37.078 --> 00:00:38.496
- Are you saying my Eagles
are one of the eight best

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:40.749
after a year of slander?
-Yeah, I'm gonna say it.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:42.584
Hey, you were the better team
on Sunday afternoon.

00:00:42.584 --> 00:00:44.210
I know that.
- Appreciate that.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.545
- And I'm so sick of hearing
about you and the Eagles.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.255
I can't even tell you.
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:49.007
- That's just the truth.
- When you watch all the games

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:51.092
on TV this weekend,
all the pregame shows

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:52.886
other than laughing
at bad jokes—no offense

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.764
to your dad, or you this
weekend, sorry—are also

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:59.225
gonna make it all about
the quarterbacks, and we get it.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.311
But it's the trenches
where games are won and lost

00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:03.772
and some of the best
offensive lines are still alive.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:05.565
- Yes.
- So these are the real matchups

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.400
for divisional round playoffs.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.110
First one, Chiefs-Colts.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.905
It's just not Andrew Luck
and Patrick Mahomes. It's—

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.490
- It's going to be
Quenton Nelson

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:14.824
the guard for
the Indianapolis Colts.

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:17.285
- All-Pro.
- All-Pro versus Chris Jones

00:01:17.285 --> 00:01:20.163
defensive tackle,
14-plus sacks.

00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:23.083
But yes, that is going to be a
huge point in the football game.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.751
The Chiefs secondary stinks.
- Yes.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.879
- You have to be able to get pressure
on Andrew Luck with your front four.

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.214
- Good luck.

00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:31.049
- Good luck gettin' there,
exactly right.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:33.051
But that will be a key matchup
that I watch

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:35.428
especially being up the middle

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.930
getting into
the quarterback's face

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.890
where he can't step up
or see passing lanes.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.642
That night, Rams-Cowboys.

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:42.769
It's gonna be about Dak
and Jared Goff.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.229
They came out
in the same draft class.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.522
- Or Gurley and Ezekiel Elliott.

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:47.023
- But what's the real matchup?

00:01:47.023 --> 00:01:48.525
- The real matchup goes up front
once again.

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:50.151
You got the Dallas Cowboys
offensive line

00:01:50.151 --> 00:01:51.694
arguably one
of the best in football

00:01:51.694 --> 00:01:52.529
arguably one
of the best in football

00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:54.614
but Zack Martin versus Aaron Donald.
Are you kidding me?

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.407
- Zack Martin was the original
Quenton Nelson.

00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:56.908
- Exactly right.

00:01:56.908 --> 00:01:57.450
- Exactly right.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.119
I would say he's the second-best
guard in football now

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.287
behind Quenton Nelson
and Aaron Donald.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.789
Come on, let's be serious.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.332
He is going to be
Defensive Player of the Year.

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:06.167
He is the best defensive player
in the league.

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:07.669
That matchup will be huge

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:10.255
because when you have
a Zack Martin

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:13.675
where a team like Dallas can go,
"We don't need to help you.

00:02:13.675 --> 00:02:16.344
We think you can handle him
by yourself," that, of course

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:18.346
frees up the rest
of the O-line to do things.

00:02:18.346 --> 00:02:20.557
But if it becomes an issue
and then they have to help—

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:23.184
- Changes the whole game.
- Then mismatches happen
in other areas.

00:02:23.184 --> 00:02:25.019
- Who wins that matchup?
- I gotta go with Aaron Donald.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:26.646
- You can't not.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.939
I was gonna yell at you
if you went Zack.

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:29.107
- He's an unstoppable force.
Right.

00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:30.900
- Patriots-Chargers.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.154
Philip Rivers, Tom Brady, oldest
matchup of quarterbacks ever.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.905
- Right.
- I'm already annoyed by it.

00:02:35.905 --> 00:02:37.240
What is the real matchup?

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.242
- I always look,
in playoff football

00:02:39.242 --> 00:02:40.994
for the New England Patriots

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:43.788
the first guy I go to other than Brady—
- Gronk.
- Is Gronk, right.

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:46.374
Gronk is the key piece
for the New England offense.

00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:48.084
- I know what you're gonna say.
- And you know.

00:02:48.084 --> 00:02:50.170
- You're gonna say there's
a Gronk-stopper on the Chargers.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.839
- There is. Derwin James is a guy
I would look at to go.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.340
That matchup will be key

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.593
not only just
in coverage too, Lefkoe.

00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:58.136
I mean, we've talked about it.

00:02:58.136 --> 00:02:59.554
Gronkowski is one of the best
blocking tight ends

00:02:59.554 --> 00:03:01.556
in the history of football,
and Derwin James

00:03:01.556 --> 00:03:05.143
plays basically middle
linebacker for the Chargers.

00:03:05.143 --> 00:03:06.769
- So his ability to—
- I'm pickin' Derwin James
in this matchup.

00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:08.855
- In the pass game,
I certainly am.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.607
I think—but the run game

00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:12.734
is where I worry
about the Chargers a little bit

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.652
but either way,
fascinating matchup.

00:03:14.652 --> 00:03:17.989
- And the Sunday night game.
Interesting.

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:19.699
- Hmm.
- It's the Saints and the Eagles.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.117
- Oh.
- And, you know

00:03:21.117 --> 00:03:22.952
did you know
that Nick Foles and Drew Brees

00:03:22.952 --> 00:03:24.412
went to the same
high school in Texas?

00:03:24.412 --> 00:03:26.206
- I did.
Austin Westlake.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.874
Yes, I was very aware of that.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.626
- You ready to hear about that
for seven hours?

00:03:29.626 --> 00:03:31.127
- Yeah.

00:03:31.127 --> 00:03:32.795
- But what's the actual matchup
in that game?

00:03:32.795 --> 00:03:34.464
- I hate to be boring,
but I'm goin' up front again.

00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:35.506
And I think that's
the great thing about

00:03:35.506 --> 00:03:36.883
the playoffs right now.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.468
We have a lot
of the top-tier D-lines

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:40.136
and offensive lines
still available.

00:03:40.136 --> 00:03:42.222
That shows you how important
it is to win those wars.

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:44.015
But your man, Fletcher Cox—

00:03:44.015 --> 00:03:46.809
- Who I believe is up there
with Aaron Donald

00:03:46.809 --> 00:03:48.394
as the best defensive tackle
in the NFL.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.563
- No doubt, yes.
- He's above Chris Jones.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:52.273
- Yes, he's—as a total player,
I agree.

00:03:52.273 --> 00:03:54.484
He is above Chris Jones.
There's no doubt about that.

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:56.319
But him versus Andrus Peat.

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.238
- Your man crush.
- My man, yes.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.949
Big legs, big butt, all of that.

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:03.743
- One of the greatest
combine body performances

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.620
in the history of the league.
- It really is fascinating.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:08.498
But he, again,
is a top-notch guard in the NFL.

00:04:08.498 --> 00:04:10.291
The Saints wanna run the ball.

00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:12.919
And again, just like we talked
with Donald and Zack Martin

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:16.256
the ability to be able to trust
a guy like Andrus Peat and go

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.883
"Oh, no, we think you can handle
Fletcher Cox by yourself"—

00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:21.010
- Now you can have
an extra receiver,
an extra running back.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:22.470
- Exactly right.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.763
You don't have to move
the offensive line

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.390
in certain directions.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.850
I think all four of these
matchups will really dictate

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.852
a lot of what goes on
in the full game.

00:04:29.852 --> 00:04:31.646
- Yeah, but you're takin',
you're takin'—

00:04:31.646 --> 00:04:33.398
You took the defender,
you're takin' Fletcher Cox?

00:04:33.398 --> 00:04:35.108
- I am taking Fletcher Cox.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.442
- Simms just said the Eagles
are gonna beat the Saints.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:37.610
- No, I didn't.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.195
Come on, Saints, let's do it!
- Stop.

00:04:39.195 --> 00:04:40.697
- I don't wanna hear
Lefkoe anymore!

00:04:40.697 --> 00:04:43.908
- Stop.
- Let's go Saints!

00:04:43.908 --> 00:04:45.952
- I'm George Kittle.
- And I'm Trent Taylor.

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:49.497
- And you're watching
"Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:04:49.497 --> 00:04:52.041
- Thank you so much, Trent Taylor
and George Kittle

00:04:52.041 --> 00:04:54.127
the second-best
football friends I know.

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:56.504
- Hey, Kittle, I heard
you been trollin' my boy

00:04:56.504 --> 00:04:59.007
Lefkoe over there—
- He DMs me.
- With DMs.

00:04:59.007 --> 00:05:01.175
You better watch it,
or I'll show you

00:05:01.175 --> 00:05:03.261
who the real king
of the arm farm is, man.

00:05:03.261 --> 00:05:04.804
You better watch it.
[Laughing]

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:08.099
- Aaron Rodgers has a new head
football coach

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:10.935
and it is the former, now,
offensive coordinator

00:05:10.935 --> 00:05:13.187
of the Titans, Matt LaFleur.

00:05:13.187 --> 00:05:16.441
Young coach that was under
Kyle Shanahan and Sean McVay

00:05:16.441 --> 00:05:18.651
and at this point,
for NFL coaches

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.571
if Sean McVay
has breathed near you

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:23.364
you're gonna be a head coach
in the NFL.

00:05:23.364 --> 00:05:25.241
- Right.
- I am very disappointed.

00:05:25.241 --> 00:05:27.785
I felt like the Titans offense
was not that great this year.

00:05:27.785 --> 00:05:29.787
If anything, I thought
Mariota regressed.

00:05:29.787 --> 00:05:31.247
Am I crazy to believe that?

00:05:31.247 --> 00:05:32.749
- I don't think you're crazy
to believe that.

00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:34.417
I wanna make sure
I get this right here.

00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:37.086
Matt LaFleur does have,
I've always thought this

00:05:37.086 --> 00:05:38.629
the potential to be
a head coach.

00:05:38.629 --> 00:05:40.173
- OK.
- He is that type of guy.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.300
I think this is way
too premature, though

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.178
to be put in this position
as the head coach

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:47.263
of Aaron Rodgers
and the Green Bay Packers.

00:05:47.263 --> 00:05:49.640
And, yes, to your point,
I would argue

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.101
the biggest weakness
of the Titans team last year

00:05:52.101 --> 00:05:54.312
was probably their pass offense.

00:05:54.312 --> 00:05:57.440
So just because you worked
for McVay or Shanahan

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.317
doesn't make you, like,
the grand master

00:05:59.317 --> 00:06:00.943
of offense as well.
- Follow-up question.

00:06:00.943 --> 00:06:02.236
- Right.
Go ahead.

00:06:02.236 --> 00:06:03.529
- Is the offense better
than the offense

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.156
that Rodgers was playing in?

00:06:05.156 --> 00:06:07.116
- Yes, he will have more ideas
than Mike McCarthy.

00:06:07.116 --> 00:06:09.702
He certainly will.
That's where McVay and Shanahan

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.454
and his background with them
will help him.

00:06:11.454 --> 00:06:13.039
But this is what people
are missing.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:15.041
- To be the head coach, though.
Like, Kyle Shanahan was an OC

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:17.752
of top-five offenses
with Matt Schaub

00:06:17.752 --> 00:06:20.630
and Andre Johnson
and the Houston Texans.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.257
- RG3.
- OK, and then he went to RG3
with the Washington Redskins.

00:06:23.257 --> 00:06:25.927
Then went to Atlanta
and had the MVP season.
- You're right.

00:06:25.927 --> 00:06:27.845
- McVay built a great offense
in Washington

00:06:27.845 --> 00:06:29.597
that took over for Shanahan—
- With Kirk Cousins, yeah.

00:06:29.597 --> 00:06:32.433
- And was one of the best
play-callers for a few years

00:06:32.433 --> 00:06:34.227
before he became the head coach.

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:36.646
So we're all just looking
for this young guy

00:06:36.646 --> 00:06:39.732
but you also gotta look at
results and facts of the matter

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:42.068
and I think that's where
it's being missed right now.

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:44.195
They're just going, like
you said, "Young? McVay?

00:06:44.195 --> 00:06:45.738
Shanahan? Hired!"

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.281
- I hope they get a good DC too

00:06:47.281 --> 00:06:49.617
but, really, my big hope—
- Keep Pettine.

00:06:49.617 --> 00:06:51.244
- Yeah, you're right.
- Right.

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:54.038
- I just wanna make sure,
if Aaron Rodgers and LaFleur

00:06:54.038 --> 00:06:55.915
are spending those late nights
in the office

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:57.667
diagramming up some plays—
- Sure.

00:06:57.667 --> 00:07:00.086
- It could be cool
if they grow together.

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:01.629
- It could be, no doubt.
- But right now, I'm underwhelmed.

00:07:01.629 --> 00:07:02.964
- It's just a little early.
I agree.

00:07:02.964 --> 00:07:04.841
- We wanted McDaniels.
- Yeah, we did.

00:07:04.841 --> 00:07:06.384
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:07:06.384 --> 00:07:07.969
- Now, I know you played
one game in the playoffs

00:07:07.969 --> 00:07:11.097
and you had a moment
that was almost spectacular.
- Right.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:12.557
- Sorry, Edell Shepherd.

00:07:12.557 --> 00:07:13.891
I don't wanna
bring up bad things.

00:07:13.891 --> 00:07:15.726
- Yeah, don't.
- But if you could imagine

00:07:15.726 --> 00:07:18.521
making an incredible play
in the playoffs

00:07:18.521 --> 00:07:20.273
it's gotta be like the greatest
feeling of all time.

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:21.774
- The playoffs in general

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.359
are the greatest feeling
of all time.

00:07:23.359 --> 00:07:25.445
I didn't even win
my playoff game.

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:28.156
I played a pretty good game
against the Washington Redskins

00:07:28.156 --> 00:07:31.659
but I knew the second I walked
into the stadium that day

00:07:31.659 --> 00:07:34.620
I said, "Man, there is something
different around here today."

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.913
Everybody's jazzed up.

00:07:35.913 --> 00:07:37.540
We came out for warm-ups

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.418
and the stadium was 80 percent full,
and I was just like

00:07:40.418 --> 00:07:43.171
"OK, we're ready for
some big-time football here."

00:07:43.171 --> 00:07:45.256
And LaVar Arrington and people
were yellin' at me

00:07:45.256 --> 00:07:46.757
and I was like,
"Wow, they're mad already

00:07:46.757 --> 00:07:48.092
and we haven't even started."

00:07:48.092 --> 00:07:49.677
So there is definitely
a different buzz.

00:07:49.677 --> 00:07:51.429
- And that's just the playoffs.
- Yeah, seriously.

00:07:51.429 --> 00:07:53.598
- So our buddy LaMarr Woodley

00:07:53.598 --> 00:07:57.101
he made one of those incredible
plays in the Super Bowl

00:07:57.101 --> 00:07:58.436
and you can just feel

00:07:58.436 --> 00:08:00.313
how awesome
it must've been to do it.

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:02.315
- I'd have a shrine in my house
just about the one play.

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:03.941
- Just for you.
- Yeah, just be like

00:08:03.941 --> 00:08:07.695
"Damn, look at what
I did to win us a Super Bowl."

00:08:07.695 --> 00:08:11.824
- I would say in, like,
the pantheon of Super Bowls

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:14.452
Steelers-Cardinals was, like,
one of the greatest

00:08:14.452 --> 00:08:16.245
most exciting games I've ever seen.
- Super Bowl 43, yeah.

00:08:16.245 --> 00:08:18.080
- You ended that Super Bowl.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.583
So, like, take me through
the play, man.

00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:22.126
Like, that s--t was nuts.

00:08:22.126 --> 00:08:23.711
- You know, it was, like,
we had a timeout before

00:08:23.711 --> 00:08:25.296
and I remember Coach Tomlin
pullin' us out, like

00:08:25.296 --> 00:08:27.131
"Woo, we need a big play."

00:08:27.131 --> 00:08:29.008
You know, that's the kinda
s--t you see on TV, in a movie.

00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:31.135
Like, "Come on, man,
we need a big play from you."

00:08:31.135 --> 00:08:33.304
Like, man, I ain't finna make
no big play.

00:08:33.304 --> 00:08:36.098
Like, "All right, Coach,
you know I got you."

00:08:36.098 --> 00:08:37.475
You know, they got
Larry Fitzgerald

00:08:37.475 --> 00:08:39.393
tallest receiver out there
at the time.

00:08:39.393 --> 00:08:40.811
Kurt Warner can throw the ball.

00:08:40.811 --> 00:08:42.271
